From d4663f18ff13fec644fde9ddbc234e9f367942ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:43:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: NAS Reject (identity-forcing cause)
 detector

Adds the `nas_reject_identity` analyzer: it flags an Attach, Tracking Area Update
or Service Reject carrying EMM cause #9 "UE identity cannot be derived by the
network" (Medium) or #10 "implicitly detached" (Low).

Cause #9 requires the UE to delete its GUTI and re-attach with its IMSI, exposing
it; a false base station that cannot authenticate the UE uses it to force
identity exposure. The Devilray study (Oh et al., 2026) found #9 the most
reliable single-cell IMSI-catching cause and reported that detectors keying
identity exposure only on an explicit Identity Request (as the Identity Request
analyzer does) miss this NAS-Reject path. Cause #10 makes the UE re-attach but
does not require discarding the GUTI, so IMSI exposure is not guaranteed -- a
weaker, far more often benign signal (lower severity).

The analyzer is STATELESS and keys on the EMM cause alone. It deliberately does
NOT claim the reject was integrity-unprotected, nor that an IMSI re-attach
followed: the NAS security-header type is not preserved through the decrypted-NAS
log, and the Attach Request's EPS mobile identity is an empty generated struct in
the current NAS parser, so neither can be read. Confirming the
unprotected-and-followed-by-IMSI case is future work gated on those two parser
capabilities. Off by default (`AnalyzerConfig` default false); #9/#10 also occur
benignly (MME restart, GUTI/MME-pool mismatch, idle-timer implicit detach), so
the severity needs per-network false-positive calibration.

Test harness: adds `emm_message()` to `analysis::test_util`. Tests cover #9
(Medium) and #10 (Low) on Attach/TAU/Service Reject, an ignored cause, a
non-reject EMM message, distinct per-cause alert text, `AnalyzerConfig`
defaulting the new key to false on an older config, and `Harness::new_with_config`
wiring the analyzer only when enabled.

Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
